course: dictionary
lesson: 9932
title: One word, many tapes
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Tape is a word with several meanings. Context tells you which one is meant. «Live shows often have small disasters, so teams keep safety pins, tape and spare costumes ready.» Safety pins and costumes are things you use to fix or stick things, so tape here means sticky tape.
explain: The same word can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a tape is a thin strip: sticky tape, red tape, finishing tape. As a verb, to tape means to stick something with tape: «She taped the box shut.» Ask yourself: is it a thing, or an action?
explain: Check the sentence. «A piece of sticky tape on a balloon can let a pin go in without a bang, because the tape stops the rubber ripping.» Tape stops the rubber from ripping, so it is holding or sticking something. Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Tape is a thin, long strip, often sticky, used to stick things together.
fact: A tape measure is a long strip with marks, used to measure length.
fact: «Tape» can also be a cassette for recording sound or video. To tape means to record.
fact: «Red tape» means too many rules and forms, and «finishing tape» is the strip a runner breaks at the end of a race.
fact: «Geckos stick to glass with millions of tiny toe hairs,» and scientists have made tape that copies them.
exercise: «Live shows often have small disasters, so teams keep safety pins, tape and spare costumes ready.» What kind of tape is meant here? | A finishing line at a race | * A thin sticky strip used to stick things together | A strip of cloth worn for a dance | A cassette for recording sound
exercise: A tape measure is used for what? | * Measuring length | Breaking the finish line | Sticking boxes shut | Recording music
exercise: «She taped the poster to the wall.» What does taped mean? | * Stuck with tape | Measured carefully | Torn into pieces | Recorded on a cassette
test: «The form needed three signatures and four stamps, which is red tape.» What does red tape mean here? | A red strip used for measuring | A sticky strip for mending paper | A prize for the fastest runner | * Too many rules and forms
test: A roll has 12 metres of tape. You cut it into 4 equal pieces. How long is each piece? | 8 metres | * 3 metres, from 12 divided by 4 | 48 metres | 3 metres
exam: «A zip has two rows of teeth on cloth tapes, and the slider pushes them together.» In this sentence, what is a tape? | To stick with tape | A cassette for recording | A tape measure | * A strip of cloth
